    summary: "The New Testament repeatedly insists that all believers are gifted. This lesson studies 1 Peter 4:10-11, 1 Corinthians 12:11-20, Romans 12:4-6, Ephesians 4:7 and Matthew 25:14-30 to see that each has received a gift to serve others, that the Spirit apportions them as he wills, that the body has many members and none is useless, that grace is given to each, and that servants are accountable for using what they are given.",
    scripture: ["1 Peter 4:10-11", "1 Corinthians 12:14-20"], more: ["1 Corinthians 12:11", "Romans 12:4-6", "Ephesians 4:7"], memory: "1 Peter 4:10",
